[ti:PyTorch 2.11: Differentiable Collectives, FlashAttention-4, and More]
[ar:Ava & Brian]
[al:PyTorch Blog Podcast]
[00:00.00]Ava: If your distributed training code needs gradients through communication, PyTorch 2.
[00:00.00]Ava：如果分布式训练代码需要让梯度穿过通信操作，PyTorch 2.
[00:06.09]11 could change what you can build.
[00:06.09]11 可能会带来新的实现方式。
[00:08.66]And if you're on Hopper or Blackwell, attention kernels may get much faster.
[00:08.66]如果你用的是 Hopper 或 Blackwell，注意力内核也可能快得多。
[00:14.23]Brian, what landed in this release?
[00:14.23]Brian，这次发布了什么？
[00:17.15]Brian: A lot, actually. PyTorch 2.
[00:17.15]Brian：其实有很多。PyTorch 2.
[00:19.15]11 has differentiable collectives, a FlashAttention-4 backend for FlexAttention, a much broader MPS story, GPU export for RNNs and LSTMs, and several device and inference improvements.
[00:19.15]11 加入了可微集合通信、FlexAttention 的 FlashAttention-4 后端、更完善的 MPS 支持、RNN 和 LSTM 的 GPU 导出，以及多项设备和推理改进。
[00:33.10]Ava: Let's start with the distributed training change.
[00:33.10]Ava：先说说分布式训练的变化。
[00:36.42]The phrase “differentiable collectives” sounds important, but also a little abstract.
[00:36.42]“可微集合通信”听起来很重要，但也有点抽象。
[00:42.52]Brian: Sure. A collective is a communication operation used by distributed workers. In 2.
[00:42.52]Brian：集合通信是分布式工作进程使用的一类通信操作。在 2.
[00:48.74]11, functional collectives can support differentiation.
[00:48.74]11 中，函数式集合通信操作支持求导。
[00:52.91]That means a training workflow can backpropagate through the collective operation itself.
[00:52.91]也就是说，训练过程可以穿过集合通信操作本身进行反向传播。
[01:00.01]Ava: Wait, so communication can now sit inside the gradient path?
[01:00.01]Ava：等等，通信操作现在也能处在梯度传播路径上？
[01:05.40]Brian: Exactly. That's the key idea.
[01:05.40]Brian：没错，这就是关键。
[01:07.50]Before this support, researchers might need custom autograd functions for some advanced workflows.
[01:07.50]以前，一些高级训练流程可能需要研究人员编写自定义 autograd 函数。
[01:14.58]With differentiable collectives, those workflows may be implemented without writing those custom functions.
[01:14.58]有了可微集合通信，这些流程或许无需自定义函数就能实现。
[01:22.67]Ava: The article calls this a significant step for distributed deep learning research and advanced training techniques.
[01:22.67]Ava：文章说，这是分布式深度学习研究和高级训练技术的一大进步。
[01:30.15]Does it promise a specific new algorithm?
[01:30.15]它有承诺支持某种具体的新算法吗？
[01:33.19]Brian: No. It doesn't name a benchmark or one particular algorithm.
[01:33.19]Brian：没有。文章没有提具体算法或基准测试。
[01:37.73]The claim is about enabling a class of training workflows.
[01:37.73]它强调的是，这项功能让一类训练流程成为可能。
[01:42.12]The feature is also listed under API-UNSTABLE, so users should expect the interface to keep changing.
[01:42.12]这项功能还被标为 API-UNSTABLE，所以接口今后可能继续变化。
[01:50.10]Ava: Got it.
[01:50.10]Ava：明白了。
[01:50.66]So the practical message is: gradients through communication are now possible, but the API isn't frozen yet.
[01:50.66]所以实际意义是：梯度现在能穿过通信操作，但 API 还没定型。
[01:59.50]Brian: Right. That's a good way to put it.
[01:59.50]Brian：对，可以这么理解。
[02:02.54]Ava: Now let's talk about attention.
[02:02.54]Ava：接着聊注意力机制。
[02:04.92]What does the new FlashAttention-4 backend actually do inside FlexAttention?
[02:04.92]新的 FlashAttention-4 后端在 FlexAttention 中具体做什么？
[02:11.12]Brian: On Hopper and Blackwell GPUs, FlexAttention can use a FlashAttention-4 backend.
[02:11.12]Brian：在 Hopper 和 Blackwell GPU 上，FlexAttention 可以使用 FlashAttention-4 后端。
[02:17.31]PyTorch can automatically generate CuTeDSL score and mask modification functions, then just-in-time instantiate FlashAttention-4 kernels.
[02:17.31]PyTorch 可以自动生成用于修改分数和掩码的 CuTeDSL 函数，再即时实例化 FlashAttention-4 内核。
[02:28.39]Ava: Can you unpack that? What should an engineer picture?
[02:28.39]Ava：能说得更具体些吗？工程师该怎么理解？
[02:32.51]Brian: Picture FlexAttention as the flexible front end.
[02:32.51]Brian：可以把 FlexAttention 看成灵活的前端。
[02:36.03]You describe how scores or masks should be modified.
[02:36.03]你描述分数或掩码该如何修改。
[02:39.84]The backend then creates specialized kernels for that description.
[02:39.84]后端再根据这套描述生成专用内核。
[02:44.69]Here, those kernels come from FlashAttention-4, using CuTeDSL, and they're instantiated just in time.
[02:44.69]这里的内核基于 FlashAttention-4，使用 CuTeDSL，并按需即时实例化。
[02:52.44]Ava: And the result is faster execution?
[02:52.44]Ava：所以运行会更快？
[02:56.06]Brian: The article reports one point two to three point two times speedups over the existing Triton implementation on compute-bound workloads.
[02:56.06]Brian：文章称，在计算密集型工作负载上，相比现有的 Triton 实现，速度提升了 1.2 到 3.2 倍。
[03:04.71]Ava: That's a wide range. So it depends heavily on the workload.
[03:04.71]Ava：这个范围挺大，看来很依赖具体工作负载。
[03:09.98]Brian: Yes. The statement is specifically for compute-bound workloads.
[03:09.98]Brian：对，这个数据专指计算密集型工作负载。
[03:14.65]We shouldn't turn it into a universal speed claim.
[03:14.65]不能说所有场景都能达到这个速度提升。
[03:18.35]Also, this backend is still under active development, and its setup details and limitations are described in a separate FlexAttention and FlashAttention-4 post.
[03:18.35]而且后端仍在积极开发中，配置细节和限制另有一篇关于 FlexAttention 和 FlashAttention-4 的文章说明。
[03:30.54]Ava: So: promising numbers, specific hardware, specific workload, and a moving API.
[03:30.54]Ava：也就是说，数据很有前景，但限定了硬件和工作负载，API 也还在变化。
[03:37.80]Brian: Exactly. Hopper and Blackwell matter here, and the feature may change as it stabilizes.
[03:37.80]Brian：没错。这里需要 Hopper 或 Blackwell，功能在稳定下来之前也可能变化。
[03:45.21]Ava: Let's move to Apple Silicon. MPS has been expanding for a while. What's new in 2. 11?
[03:45.21]Ava：再聊聊 Apple Silicon。MPS 一直在扩展，2.11 有什么新变化？
[03:53.29]Brian: MPS gets error reporting support and more operator coverage.
[03:53.29]Brian：MPS 增加了错误报告支持，也支持了更多算子。
[03:58.25]New distribution functions include log_normal, cauchy, and geometric.
[03:58.25]新增的分布函数包括 log_normal、cauchy 和 geometric。
[04:03.95]There are also operator migrations, such as erfcx, and grid_sampler_2d now supports all operation modes.
[04:03.95]还有 erfcx 等算子迁移到了 MPS；grid_sampler_2d 现在支持所有操作模式。
[04:12.55]Finally, baddbmm and addbmm are extended to integer and complex types.
[04:12.55]最后，baddbmm 和 addbmm 扩展了对整数和复数类型的支持。
[04:18.69]Ava: The error reporting sounds especially useful. What problem does it catch?
[04:18.69]Ava：错误报告听起来特别实用。它能发现什么问题？
[04:24.35]Brian: Asynchronous error reporting can detect out-of-bounds access during GPU indexing operations.
[04:24.35]Brian：异步错误报告能检测 GPU 索引操作中的越界访问。
[04:30.98]The article gives an example where an MPS tensor is indexed with an invalid index, and torch.
[04:30.98]文章举了个例子：用无效索引访问 MPS 张量时，torch.
[04:37.69]mps. synchronize raises an index-out-of-bounds error.
[04:37.69]mps.synchronize 会抛出索引越界错误。
[04:41.86]Ava: So the failure might surface when you synchronize, rather than exactly where the indexing line runs.
[04:41.86]Ava：所以错误可能在同步时才显现，而不是恰好在执行索引那一行时。
[04:48.93]Brian: Right. That's the important debugging detail.
[04:48.93]Brian：对，这正是调试时的关键细节。
[04:52.22]GPU work can be asynchronous, and synchronization is where the error is reported in that example.
[04:52.22]GPU 操作可能是异步的；在这个例子中，错误会在同步时报告。
[04:59.67]Ava: Next, export support.
[04:59.67]Ava：接下来聊导出支持。
[05:01.61]The release says RNN modules, including LSTM and GRU, can now be exported on GPUs.
[05:01.61]发布说明称，LSTM 和 GRU 等 RNN 模块现在可以在 GPU 上导出。
[05:09.18]Why does that matter?
[05:09.18]这有什么意义？
[05:11.47]Brian: It broadens the model types that can be deployed with torch.
[05:11.47]Brian：这让更多类型的模型可以通过 torch.
[05:15.88]export for production inference.
[05:15.88]export 导出，用于生产环境推理。
[05:18.23]In addition, tracing LSTM with dynamic shapes is now supported.
[05:18.23]此外，现在也支持以动态形状追踪 LSTM。
[05:23.22]Ava: And the GRU API stays the same?
[05:23.22]Ava：GRU API 还是一样的吗？
[05:26.37]Brian: Yes. The article says the GRU API is unchanged, while the new API is LSTM.
[05:26.37]Brian：是的。文章说 GRU API 没有变化，新 API 针对的是 LSTM。
[05:32.62]So teams working with recurrent models get a larger export path without an API change for GRU.
[05:32.62]因此，使用循环模型的团队有了更广的导出选择，而无需更改 GRU API。
[05:40.91]Ava: That sounds practical for production teams. What else is happening on AMD GPUs?
[05:40.91]Ava：这对生产团队很实用。AMD GPU 还有什么新变化？
[05:47.59]Brian: ROCm gets device-side assertions, which should improve debugging.
[05:47.59]Brian：ROCm 增加了设备端断言，应该能让调试更方便。
[05:52.49]It also gets significant TopK optimizations and radix-select improvements.
[05:52.49]它还大幅优化了 TopK，并改进了基数选择。
[05:58.06]Those improvements cache data in shared memory, helping both developer experience and performance on AMD GPUs.
[05:58.06]这些改进将数据缓存在共享内存中，有助于改善开发体验并提升 AMD GPU 的性能。
[06:06.69]Ava: Let's switch vendors again. What's XPU Graph?
[06:06.69]Ava：再换一家厂商。XPU Graph 是什么？
[06:11.09]Brian: XPU Graph is for Intel GPUs.
[06:11.09]Brian：XPU Graph 面向 Intel GPU。
[06:13.54]It captures a sequence of XPU operations into a runtime execution graph.
[06:13.54]它把一系列 XPU 操作捕获为运行时执行图。
[06:19.83]You can replay that graph multiple times.
[06:19.83]这个图可以重复执行多次。
[06:23.76]Ava: And replaying avoids repeated overhead?
[06:23.76]Ava：重复执行就能避免反复产生开销？
[06:27.15]Brian: Yes.
[06:27.15]Brian：对。
[06:27.48]It reduces CPU overhead, including kernel-launch overhead and Python-runtime overhead.
[06:27.48]它能降低 CPU 开销，包括内核启动和 Python 运行时的开销。
[06:34.56]The goal is better workload performance on Intel GPUs.
[06:34.56]目标是提升 Intel GPU 上的工作负载性能。
[06:39.00]The article points users to the API documentation for usage details.
[06:39.00]文章建议用户查阅 API 文档，了解具体用法。
[06:44.95]Ava: There's also FP16 GEMM on CPUs through OpenBLAS. Is that mainly for servers?
[06:44.95]Ava：CPU 上也能通过 OpenBLAS 使用 FP16 GEMM。这主要面向服务器吗？
[06:52.79]Brian: The article frames it as useful for CPU-based deployments, especially edge devices and CPU-only inference scenarios.
[06:52.79]Brian：文章认为它适用于基于 CPU 的部署，尤其是边缘设备和纯 CPU 推理场景。
[07:01.85]OpenBLAS now provides FP16 half-precision GEMM support there, which can make FP16 inference faster.
[07:01.85]OpenBLAS 现在为这些场景提供 FP16 半精度 GEMM 支持，可加快 FP16 推理。
[07:09.94]Ava: Now, a release detail that can break build environments: CUDA.
[07:09.94]Ava：接下来是一个可能影响构建环境的发布变更：CUDA。
[07:15.33]Brian: Starting with 2.
[07:15.33]Brian：从 2.
[07:16.70]11, CUDA 13 is the default installed version for both x86_64 and ARM platforms.
[07:16.70]11 版起，x86_64 和 ARM 平台默认安装 CUDA 13。
[07:23.47]Users who need another build can still use CPU-only packages or CUDA 12.
[07:23.47]需要其他构建版本的用户，仍可使用纯 CPU 软件包或 CUDA 12.
[07:29.63]8 builds from the relevant wheel subfolders.
[07:29.63]8 构建版本，可从相应的 wheel 子目录获取。
[07:33.75]Ava: So upgrading may mean checking which CUDA wheel your deployment expects.
[07:33.75]Ava：所以升级时可能需要检查部署环境要求哪个 CUDA wheel。
[07:39.41]Brian: Yes, especially if your environment is pinned to CUDA 12. 8.
[07:39.41]Brian：对，尤其是环境固定使用 CUDA 12.8 的情况。
[07:44.46]Ava: And TorchScript?
[07:44.46]Ava：TorchScript 呢？
[07:46.59]Brian: TorchScript was deprecated in 2. 10. The guidance is to use torch.
[07:46.59]Brian：TorchScript 已在 2.10 版弃用。建议使用 torch.
[07:51.78]export instead of the jit trace and script APIs, and to use ExecuTorch instead of the embedded runtime.
[07:51.78]export 取代 jit 的 trace 和 script API，并用 ExecuTorch 取代嵌入式运行时。
[08:00.23]Ava: So 2. 11 reinforces a migration that's already underway.
[08:00.23]Ava：所以 2.11 进一步推动了已经开始的迁移。
[08:06.29]Brian: That's right.
[08:06.29]Brian：没错。
[08:07.22]The release blog points readers to a PTC talk for more detail, but the main direction is clear: torch.
[08:07.22]发布博客推荐读者观看 PTC 演讲了解详情，但主要方向很明确：用 torch.
[08:14.50]export for export workflows, and ExecuTorch for the embedded runtime.
[08:14.50]export 处理导出工作流，用 ExecuTorch 作为嵌入式运行时。
[08:19.77]Ava: How large was this release effort?
[08:19.77]Ava：这次发布投入了多少工作？
[08:23.05]Brian: The release includes 2,723 commits from 432 contributors since PyTorch 2. 10.
[08:23.05]Brian：自 PyTorch 2.10 以来，这次发布汇集了 432 位贡献者的 2,723 次提交。
[08:29.86]The project thanks the community and encourages users to try the changes and report issues.
[08:29.86]项目组感谢社区，并鼓励用户试用这些更新、报告问题。
[08:38.26]Ava: And the release rhythm is changing too.
[08:38.26]Ava：发布节奏也在变化。
[08:41.46]Brian: For 2026, PyTorch moves from quarterly releases to one release every two months.
[08:41.46]Brian：2026 年，PyTorch 将从每季度发布一次改为每两个月发布一次。
[08:47.44]That means users may see features arrive more often, but they'll also need to track compatibility more closely.
[08:47.44]这意味着新功能可能更频繁地推出，用户也需要更密切地关注兼容性。
[08:56.09]Ava: Before we close, give me the three points I should remember.
[08:56.09]Ava：结束前，说说我该记住的三个要点。
[09:00.88]Brian: First, differentiable functional collectives let gradients pass through collective operations, opening advanced distributed-training workflows without custom autograd functions.
[09:00.88]Brian：第一，可微的函数式集合通信让梯度能够穿过集合通信操作，无需自定义 autograd 函数即可支持更高级的分布式训练工作流。
[09:13.43]Second, FlexAttention can use FlashAttention-4 on Hopper and Blackwell, with reported one point two to three point two times speedups on compute-bound workloads, while the backend remains under active development.
[09:13.43]第二，FlexAttention 可以在 Hopper 和 Blackwell 上使用 FlashAttention-4。据报告，计算受限的工作负载可提速 1.2 到 3.2 倍，但该后端仍在持续开发中。
[09:28.52]Third, 2.
[09:28.52]第三，2。
[09:29.16]11 expands deployment and hardware support: MPS operators and error reporting, GPU export for RNNs and LSTMs, ROCm debugging and TopK work, Intel XPU Graph, and CPU FP16 GEMM.
[09:29.16]11 扩展了部署和硬件支持：MPS 算子及错误报告、RNN 和 LSTM 的 GPU 导出、ROCm 调试和 TopK 改进、Intel XPU Graph，以及 CPU FP16 GEMM。
[09:41.91]Ava: And the migration notes are CUDA 13 by default, TorchScript deprecated, and releases every two months in 2026.
[09:41.91]Ava：迁移时还要注意：默认使用 CUDA 13，TorchScript 已弃用，2026 年每两个月发布一个版本。
[09:51.67]Brian: Exactly.
[09:51.67]Brian：没错。
[09:52.29]Check the current documentation before relying on the API-UNSTABLE features, and report issues as you try them.
[09:52.29]使用标记为 API-UNSTABLE 的功能前，请先查看最新文档；试用时遇到问题也请反馈。
[10:01.21]Ava: That's PyTorch 2. 11.
[10:01.21]Ava：以上就是 PyTorch 2.11。
[10:02.80]Thanks for listening, and we'll be back with another paper-to-practice conversation.
[10:02.80]感谢收听，我们下期再聊如何把论文成果用于实践。
